@ENDNODE


@NODE "faq" "MorphUAE - FAQ"
@PREV "usageprefs"
@NEXT "news"

@{b}@{u}FAQ - Frequently Asked Questions@{uu}@{ub}

* @{b}Q = Question@{ub}
* @{b}A = Answer@{ub}

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Q - Where can I find Amiga ROM files?

A - Easiest way is to buy a licence from www.amigaforever.com
    The cheapest way is to obtain them for Android (via Google Play) :
    https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.cloanto.amigaforever.essentials

    If you already have a real Amiga you can dump the content of the kickstart
    directly from it and use that in the emulator. There are several tools on
    Aminet for this purpose.


Q - The render GUI doesn't show the correct colours and the graphics look weird?

A - This emulator NEEDS 24bit resolution to be able to work as intended.


Q - The mouse position on the Amiga (emulation) side is not fully in sync with 
    the host mouse co-ordinates?

A - This issue needs to be adressed in future versions of MorphUAE and it's an
    already known issue.


Q - When using the fullscreen mode the graphics are not as "large" as expected, 
    how come?

A - Add a 24/32 bit screenmode with the resolution 640 x 512 pixels in the 
    monitor preferences and the screen should fill it up better.


Q - Can I use the P96 driver for RTG software with MorphUAE?

A - No, not at this point.
    The main idea behind this emulator is to have compability with games & 
    demos back from the Amiga days. Apart from that, system friendly RTG 
    programs runs straight into MorphOS directly. So, there is nothing really
    to gain by adding this into the emulator. Maybe one day, but it's not at 
    all on the priority list.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------


@ENDNODE

@NODE "news" "MorphUAE - What's new?"
@PREV "usage"
@NEXT "history"

 @{b}@{u}What's new@{uu}@{ub}

 · Now the requesters keeps track of which ADF file and path is selected on
   each image device. (Suggested by jPV)

 · Drag and drop multiple ADF images distribute them over several devices.
   (Suggested by jPV)

 · ADF Image LED is now shown in a BLUE colour if there is an image
   mounted to it. (Suggested by jPV)

 · Added an CLI/Shell option to enable overscan resolution (-overscan).

 · The reset button can now also change machine type, via a popup menu.
   (Suggested by bitRocky)

 · The current active ADF image is also shown in the window title.
   (Suggested by bitRocky)

 · Mounted virtual devices was not fully freed when switching between
   machine types.

 · Tooltypes can be used to change behaviour of the emulation.

 · Savestates can now be saved or loaded from the GUI.

@ENDNODE

